      "created_at": "2018-10-23T09:27:40Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-23T09:27:40Z",
      "body": "Well, in the `users` table, there is the email, firstname, lastname. Then there is phone, cellphone, skype, website, but these are not mandatory fields. Also, I'll probably change them at some point because they are a bit pointless…\r\n\r\nRest of the app is just integers mostly.\r\n\r\nThere is a anti brute force system, but it logs a hash of the IP + UserAgent, so not identifiable info.\r\n\r\nThen there is the nginx webserver in the container that logs the IP address with the time for each requests (in /var/log/nginx/access.log).\r\n\r\n> maybe there are some \"hidden\" logs such as revisions with name and time which may be connected to Issue #924.\r\n\r\nThis would be a pointer to the users row anyway, so just a number.",
