      "updated_at": "2021-10-20T10:04:09Z",
      "body": ">  Is there a variable that can be queried if the user logs in for the first time?\r\n\r\nYes there is `last_login` that is null at first.\r\n\r\nAlso, I know a service that does the privacy policy step at the IDP level, so maybe that could also be a solution for you: when you login to a service for the first time, you have to accept the terms of use for that service.",
